**POST /api/v1/memos**

The mapping is declared on the `CreateMemo` RPC in `proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto:21-25`:

```proto
rpc CreateMemo(CreateMemoRequest) returns (Memo) {
  option (google.api.http) = {
    post: "/api/v1/memos"
    body: "memo"
  };
```

The request body is the `memo` field (`body: "memo"`), i.e. a `Memo` message rather than the full `CreateMemoRequest`; the optional `memo_id` field (`proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto:299`) therefore travels as a query parameter. Server-side the RPC lands on `v1.APIV1Service.CreateMemo` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:70`), with the Connect handler wrapper at `server/router/api/v1/connect_services.go:306`.
